            <ArticleTitle>Synthesis of an Uncharged Tetra-cyclopeptide Acting as a Transmembrane Carrier: Enhanced Cellular and Nuclear Uptake.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>612-615</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.orglett.6b03776</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A small uncharged cyclopeptide scaffold inspired by a natural product and designed to undergo postfunctionalizations was used as a new transmembrane vector. A bioactive and fluorescent triazole aminocoumarin was bound to this carrier to facilitate its moving across cell and subcellular membranes, and this led to an increase in its cell toxicity.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
